    max [TV(Q_C,Q_P) - p]            = +2.220e-16  (must be <= 0)
    max [p - beta(C)]                = +2.220e-16  (must be <= 0)
    max [p - beta^P(C)]              = +1.110e-16  (must be <= 0)
    max [|int g d(d_C - d_P)| - (L-1)p] = +2.114e-16  (must be <= 0)
    max [beta^P(C) - L p]            = +4.441e-16  (must be <= 0)
    max [beta(C) - L p]              = +4.441e-16  (must be <= 0)
(B) proof of Prop. 2.3: max [int TV(P,C_u) d d_Ct - L beta(C_u) - (L-1) beta(C_t)] = +2.220e-16 (<= 0)

